    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0820" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-11T20:00:00-04:00">September 11, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>358. Department’s 347, August 31, noon.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d633-f1"/> Please
                    telegraph action taken and substance of any further communication whether
                    written or oral that has been received by the Embassy from the Foreign Office.
                    Do not make any new approach to Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>The Department is informed on private authority that the British and the
                    Netherland Governments have already made representations <pb facs="0821" n="731"
                        xml:id="pg731"/> to the Japanese Government, and by the Netherland Legation
                    at Washington that the Netherland Government has instructed its Minister at
                    Tokyo to make friendly representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d633-f1" n="31" xml:id="d633-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see last paragraph of telegram No. 151, August 31, 5 p.m., to
                    the Ambassador in Japan, <ref target="#pg728">p. 728</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
